e you have that break you get each  issue you get you've got a month from  one that comes out until the next one  comes out to digest everything you got I  mean that's  my watchman is so dense you actually was  actually going to be worth it for you to  keep coming back to this thing over the  course of a month until the next station  came out but also because each issue is  closed off it allowed each issue to  delve into something very specific  whether it was the history of the  Minutemen whether it was Rorschach's  mental state whether it was the origin  of dr. Manhattan and just zero in on  that and only deal with that film  doesn't really work like that  don't you really kind of need more of a  through-line for it to work I I don't  they need that like it's an absolute but  that's what film does well film does  does essentially focus forward momentum  very well and that's not watchman but  sort of being able to do it as episodes  you know closed off the way that the  issues are closed off that is closer to  it and would allow you to have honoring  the source material actually work  because as I said the movie was very  true to the source material in terms of  recreating the imagery and using the  same words but because it was so  tailored to that original medium it just  it loses its strength now unfortunately  I think we've hit a point now even  though a miniseries or TV series is what  they should have done in the first place  I actually think it's now not worth  doing it because the movie has already  come out again not because oh the movie  did as well as it can do it but because  because the movie is so accurate to the  original comics in terms of you know  what it presents up there  even though I feel it doesn't work all  you can do is basically present the same  thing Zack Snyder already presented but  just do it in a format that is more  appropriate because it really is so  direct the visual point of reference the  story point of reference the character  references were translated so directly  you know improving the narrative I don't  think is going to be enough because  we're going to be showing going yeah I  saw this maybe this is a little better  but I'm getting the same thing again and  I feel like the movie kind of I feel  like we it was going to be that accurate  we were only going to get one shot at it  and the  movie was the shy and again I personally  don't think it worked because this isn't  a case where the movie happened and it  got everything wrong so we're going to  do the miniseries that do it right which  was the theory behind something like say  Stephen King's The Shining miniseries  now that's not me saying the shining is  better than the movie but that's me say  there was a validity in that because so  much was changed up in the movie version  that Stephen King said no let's do  something that's much more accurate and  so you know they were able to do that  now the obvious solution to that would  be to change stuff so that it makes it  worth revisiting again but Watchmen  doesn't hold up to that B and part of  what got me started thinking about this  again was actually seeing spider-man  homecoming because I said in my review  that I liked all of the changes that  were done to specific characters to some  of the Lord to Peter himself and his  home situation and everything I liked  pretty much all the changes and part of  the reason I like the changes was  because with Sam Raimi's movie it his  first two movies at least we got really  comic accurate representation of these  characters Arlene you know sort of their  initial 60s early 70s versions of these  characters it was incredibly comic  accurate to those in terms of how Peter  behaved how Flash behaves Mary Jane Aunt  May Uncle Ben the Green Goblin Harry all  of it it felt like it was lifted  directly out of the books and visually  it felt a lot like that too  so since we already had our super comic  accurate version of spider-man I was  actually quite relieved and engaged to  see spider-man home company a home home  company I think I said that in my review  to homecoming play with these elements a  little bit more and do something a  little more different with them and  that's the sort of thing I would have  resisted if spider-man homecoming was  the first movie version of spider-man we  had  I wouldn't have been accepting of those  changes because I would have been like  well can't we get you know the accurate  version first well since we did now  there's fine now you'd think that would  mean I'd be going well with Watchmen now  do a more looser version you'll have the  freedom to do that except is a big  difference between Watchmen and  spider-man and that is Spiderman had  decades got about fifty years about of  history to him in terms of you know  stories and characters and ways the the  main character has been interpreted and  things that have happened to him so  there's a lot to pull from and because  it's changed so much it's hardly even  said that there is a definitive version  of spider-man and like I said even Sam  Raimi's version was definitive to a -  you know the version OHSO having he grew  up reading but that's not the case with  Watchmen there is a definitive watchman  there's only one watchman story yes I  know they made the extra stuff before  Watchmen but are any of us really  bringing that on board  really I suppose that Oh HBO could bring  that in for additional material I don't  think that's worth doing but again my  point is Watchmen for as long as it's  been out is just the one narrative you  don't have the freedom to go oh well see  well back when we did it last time it  was that bill and that will do this  other villain that wasn't in the last no  it's the same story and it has to be the  same story because it's not the same  story that it's not Watchmen anymore  anymore Watchmen is not just a thematic  sir it is a meticulous story down to the  fine details everything in that book  means something feeds into something and  is there for a reason  now that's not me saying absolutely  every detail has to be recreated but it  does mean that you cannot just  willy-nilly start changing stuff because  everything matters every brick in this  building matters you start poking at  something the whole thing could easily  come down  everything in that book is a  load-bearing brick which probably isn't  a thing I don't know construction but I  hope you get what I'm saying there and  if you can't differentiate it from the  movie it's going to not feel like it's  an endeavor worth taking but to  differentiate it from the movie is it's  just going to wreck it is just going to  the things that they would have to do to  make it different from the movie would  just not would most likely make the  story not work anymore because I mean  just to be blunt about it no matter who  they get to make this thing and I  believe it's Damon Lindelof working on  it um Damon Lindelof I you sir are not  Alan Moore um if you're going to go in  and try and add new material and make it  seem like Alan Moore it's not going to  work you want to our recent comparison  for that look at the additional stuff  that was written for the look for the  animated version of The Killing Joke you  can tell you can draw a hard line  between the stuff that was written by  other people on namely Brian Azzarello  and the stuff that was lifted directly  from the comic ie essentially written by  Alan Moore huge staggering difference  Alan Moore who it sounds like I worship  at the altar of Alan Moore Alan Moore is  not a flawless person he's not even a  flawless writer but he's an incredibly  good writer and when he is on he's kind  of unimpeachable and he was definitely  on when he wrote Watchmen so if you  can't change it but the movie version we  already got which was widely seen I mean  I know it underperformed - what the  Warner Brothers had hoped but a lot of  people know it certainly the fans all  know it and we've already gotten it and  that you know retained everything and  made it look like Washington sound like  Watchmen what the mini fear is going to  do just add in more details but it's  just going to be  it's just going to be the same thing  longer again it's going to feel like the  super extended cut of the movie now  maybe there's another angle that they  can take with that but again it Watchmen  is not a story that lends itself to I've  got a new spin on this a lot of comic  books are super your comic books  especially anything long-running there's  a ton of room to reinterpret go in there  give it your own spin not Watchmen  though it's just it's it is a singular  work it really is and I think it's an  amazing piece of work and if the movie  had never been made I would be so  cautiously pumped for the idea of an HBO  series but the movie happened and the  movie happened  visually superficially very accurate to  the comic and I think that makes it  impossible now to make a TV version  that's going to be worth seeing because  it's either going to feel like the same  thing again or it's not going to feel  like Watchmen so there's me doing that  thing I often do which is uh to just say  why something that other people are  getting excited about it's probably  gonna suck I don't mean to be this  negative I really don't  it's what my brain does and sometimes I  spell that out and you folks get it  sorry  in any Katie says my thoughts on the  possibility of Watchmen becoming a TV  series on HBO what are your thoughts on  it and exactly what way do you think I  am a massive idiot if you can do so  without wishing death upon me or wit or  any other bodily harm go ahead and leave  your comments down below let's talk  about it don't forget to like subscribe  check me out on Twitter at council of  geeks give a listen to the council of  geeks podcast available on itunes  stitcher i am also one half of the punch  like a girl podcast also available on  i